OL,3,GNEWSAResidents disgusted by fly-tipping
OL,4,A'free for all'
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople living on an estate say they are
OL,7,Fdisgusted by a large pile of waste,
OL,8,Fwhich they describe as a fly-tipping
OL,9,F"free for all".
OL,11,FResidents on the Ermine West estate, in
OL,12,FLincoln, said the rubbish, including a
OL,13,Fmattress, bedstead, clothes, a
OL,14,Fpushchair and broken glass, had been
OL,15,Fdumped on a green patch of land about a
OL,16,Fweek ago and added to since.
OL,18,FTony Brien said he had reported the
OL,19,Fwaste to the council and added: "People
OL,20,Fsee one item and think they can throw
OL,21,Fmore on top."
OL,23,APub: 29-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
